#### **Lot Variation Resolution Logic** (lotVariation.service.ts:21-60)

```typescript
// Line 21-60: Priority-based lot lookup
async findLotByNumberOrVariation(
  lotNumber: string,
  tx?: Prisma.TransactionClient,
): Promise<(Lot & { recipe?: any }) | null> {
  const client = tx || this.prismaRead;

  // CHANGED (TEC-1047): Check variation mapping FIRST
  // This ensures we always use canonical lots when variations exist
  const variation = await client.lotVariation.findFirst({
    where: { variationNumber: lotNumber },  // Line 33: Search by variation
    include: {
      canonicalLot: {
        include: { recipe: true },
      },
    },
  });

  if (variation) {
    // Line 38-42: Found variation mapping
    this.logger.log(
      `Found lot via variation: ${lotNumber} -> ${variation.canonicalLot.lotNumber}`,
    );
    return variation.canonicalLot;  // Return canonical, not variation
  }

  // FALLBACK: Try exact match on lot number
  // Line 45-52: If no variation, try exact lot match
  const exactLot = await client.lot.findFirst({
    where: { lotNumber },
    include: { recipe: true },
  });

  if (exactLot) {
    this.logger.log(`Found exact lot match: ${lotNumber}`);
  }

  return exactLot;
}
```

**Lookup Decision Tree**:
```
Input: lotNumber (extracted from serial)
  │
  ├─ Step 1: Query LotVariation table
  │  WHERE variationNumber = lotNumber
  │  │
  │  ├─ FOUND? → Return canonicalLot (line 42)
  │  │  Example: "25D23P" in variation table
  │  │         → Returns lot record for "25D23P.01"
  │  │
  │  └─ NOT FOUND? → Proceed to Step 2
  │
  └─ Step 2: Query Lot table (fallback)
     WHERE lotNumber = lotNumber
     │
     ├─ FOUND? → Return exact lot match
     │
     └─ NOT FOUND? → Return null (lot doesn't exist)
```

