## Answer to Question 34

**How does the warehouse job aggregated staging work?**

Warehouse job aggregated staging **consolidates staging records from a parent job and all its child jobs into a unified view**, with color-coded job context and flexible filtering for issue resolution workflows.

### 1. **Aggregation Strategy** (`apps/whk-wms/src/warehouseJobs/base/warehouse-jobs.service.ts:4490-4520`)

```typescript
async getAggregatedStagingRecords(
  jobId: string,
  status?: string,
  hasIssues?: boolean,
  issueTypes?: string[],
  issueFilterLogic?: "AND" | "OR",
  issueLevels?: string[],
): Promise<{
  records: Array<any & { jobId: string; jobTitle: string; jobColor: string }>;
  count: number;
  jobSummary: Array<{
    jobId: string;
    jobTitle: string;
    jobColor: string;
    total: number;
    occupied: number;
    empty: number;
    status: string;
  }>;
}> {
  // Get the parent job
  const parentJob = await this.prisma.warehouseJobs.findUnique({
    where: { id: jobId, deleted: false },
    select: {
      id: true,
      title: true,
      childJobsCount: true,
    },
  });

  if (!parentJob) {
    throw new NotFoundException(`Warehouse job with ID ${jobId} not found`);
  }

  // Get all child job IDs recursively
  const childJobIds = await this.getChildJobIdsRecursive(jobId);
  const allJobIds = [jobId, ...childJobIds];

  // Fetch all jobs to get titles, status, and assign colors
  const jobs = await this.prisma.warehouseJobs.findMany({
    where: {
      id: { in: allJobIds },
      deleted: false,
    },
    select: {
      id: true,
      title: true,
      status: true,
    },
    orderBy: {
      createdAt: "asc",
    },
  });

  // Create job color mapping with status
  const jobColorMap = new Map<string, { title: string; color: any; status: string }>();
  jobs.forEach((job, index) => {
    jobColorMap.set(job.id, {
      title: job.title,
      color: this.getJobColor(index),  // Color assigned by job order
      status: job.status,
    });
  });
}
```

**Three-step aggregation**:
1. Fetch parent job metadata
2. Get all child job IDs recursively
3. Assign colors to jobs based on their creation order

### 2. **Flexible Filtering** (`warehouse-jobs.service.ts:4550-4610`)

```typescript
// Build where clause for filtering
const where: any = {
  warehouseJobId: { in: allJobIds },  // All jobs in hierarchy
};

if (status) {
  where.processingStatus = status;  // Filter by staging status
}

if (hasIssues !== undefined) {
  where.hasIssues = hasIssues;  // Filter records with/without issues
}

// Build issue filter conditions
const issueConditions: any = {};

if (issueTypes && issueTypes.length > 0) {
  issueConditions.errorType = { in: issueTypes };
}

if (issueLevels && issueLevels.length > 0) {
  issueConditions.errorLevel = { in: issueLevels };
}

// Add combined filter with AND/OR logic
if (
  (issueTypes && issueTypes.length > 0) ||
  (issueLevels && issueLevels.length > 0)
) {
  const logic = issueFilterLogic || "OR";

  if (logic === "OR") {
    // OR logic: Records that have ANY matching issue
    where.issues = {
      some: issueConditions,
    };
  } else {
    // AND logic: Records that have ALL selected issue types
    if (issueTypes && issueTypes.length > 0) {
      where.AND = issueTypes.map((type) => ({
        issues: {
          some: {
            errorType: type,
            ...(issueLevels &&
              issueLevels.length > 0 && {
                errorLevel: { in: issueLevels },
              }),
          },
        },
      }));
    }
  }
}

// Fetch staging records with filters
const stagingRecords = await this.prisma.inventoryCheckStaging.findMany({
  where,
  include: {
    issues: {
      orderBy: { errorLevel: "desc" },
    },
  },
  orderBy: [{ hasIssues: "desc" }, { createdAt: "asc" }],
});
```

**Five filtering dimensions**:
1. **Status**: Filter by `processingStatus` (PENDING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, etc.)
2. **Has Issues**: Boolean flag for records with/without issues
3. **Issue Types**: Comma-separated error types (BarrelNoLabel, OrphanBarrelPrior, etc.)
4. **Issue Levels**: Comma-separated severity levels (CRITICAL, ERROR, WARN, INFO)
5. **Filter Logic**: AND (all issue types) vs OR (any issue type)

